hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2668","Muhammad bin Al-Ala' bin Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Hafs (i.e., Ibn Ghiyath) narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) ordered a Muhrim (a pilgrim in the state of Ihram) to kill a snake in the Sacred Sanctuary (Al-Haram)."
